            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "ac8121aa-5c0c-47cf-adc8-06a17a05e80a",
               "text": "Original text",
               "page": "index.html?page=class_content&arg=a358881b-26e5-45c8-9d1e-e89a161096c7",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2026",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "Can we represent the stages of learning (pre-sciences, proto-sciences, and sciences) with the Matryoshka (матрёшка) doll?",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "81808640-c7df-47c4-95cf-fbbfeca4c456",
         "prev": "",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": "yes",
         "score": 2
      },
      {
         "id": "81808640-c7df-47c4-95cf-fbbfeca4c456",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "happy",
         "source_menu": [
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "cd61bc64-1358-4bfd-b343-3629facaa3b4",
               "text": "González Redondo, Francisco A.",
               "page": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RFui5Z52pUY",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2024",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            },
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "ac8121aa-5c0c-47cf-adc8-06a17a05e80a",
               "text": "Original text",
               "page": "index.html?page=class_content&arg=a358881b-26e5-45c8-9d1e-e89a161096c7",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2026",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Playing and living\n\nThe dolls shown at the beginning of the lesson, with which some children play when they are little, are connected to our learning.\n\nThe smallest doll is the pre-science phase, in which we learn letters, numbers, and what a day is.\n\nThe second doll, which has the smallest one inside it, is the proto-science phase, in which we learn to describe life with texts, to represent what we see with formulas, and we see that a day is more than the time in which we see the sun.\n\nThe third doll has the other two inside it and is the science stage. In it, we learn the origin of words, the foundation for formulas, and that we are all star dust.\n\nAnd, since knowledge never stops, the fourth, the fifth, and other upper dolls are added as we learn more and more.",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "c33765d4-e5ce-4384-9cbc-86a7768f790f",
